      "math_academy_id": "q-125510",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{3}}{64}, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & x\\ge 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=F(m)=\\frac{{m}^{3}}{64},\\,0\\le m\\le 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{m}^{3}}{64}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⇒\\,m=\\sqrt[3]{32}.\n$$",
